{"candidateAnswer":"Pomodoro technique","evidence":"[D18:3 | 3:59 pm on 16 November, 2023] Tim: Ouch, bummer about the injury. Hang tight. This week has been swamped with exams for me but I'm plowing through.\n[D18:7 | 3:59 pm on 16 November, 2023] Tim: That's cool! I like breaking up my studying into smaller parts. 25 minutes on, then 5 minutes off for something fun. It's less overwhelming and keeps me on track.","itemId":"urn:uuid:b8d9081e-11b2-5aa4-b455-ec74e5f07e8c","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:caccd49fcb1921eae05fc51fdc89405f2f81db5606b1f229e94e2562307d6da5","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which popular time management technique does Tim use to prepare for exams?","referenceAnswer":"Pomodoro technique","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"caccd49fcb1921eae05fc51fdc89405f2f81db5606b1f229e94e2562307d6da5"}}]}